WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.430
On-site assessment compares the forecast with actual conditions at the place and time of

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:04.851
flight.

00:00:04.851 --> 00:00:09.635
Record wind direction, average behavior, gusts, temperature, visibility, precipitation,

00:00:09.635 --> 00:00:11.341
clouds, sun, and signs of change.

00:00:11.341 --> 00:00:12.840
Observe terrain and structures.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.980
Flags, trees, water, dust, smoke, drifting precipitation,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.040
and cloud movement can reveal local effects.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.680
A sheltered staging area may hide the wind or turbulence along the route.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:26.420
Inspect launch and recovery surfaces for water, snow, ice, dust, loose debris, mud, slope,

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.217
and crew footing.

00:00:27.217 --> 00:00:31.010
Confirm emergency landing areas remain available and that people, vehicles,

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.860
or activity have not changed the plan.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.355
Brief the crew on current conditions, thresholds, route, battery reserve,

00:00:36.355 --> 00:00:39.710
communication terms, landing options, and abort criteria.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.345
Everyone should understand that raising a concern is expected,

00:00:42.345 --> 00:00:44.460
not an obstacle to mission completion.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.220
Conditions must be monitored during flight.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.145
Watch aircraft attitude, groundspeed, battery use, signal, image quality, precipitation,

00:00:51.145 --> 00:00:53.180
visibility, and changing ground activity.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.425
Trends matter before an alert becomes critical.

00:00:55.425 --> 00:00:59.060
If actual conditions differ materially from the plan, pause and reassess.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:02.125
A decision made at the office does not obligate the crew to launch.

00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:05.525
Record the final go, delay, modification, or cancellation and why.

00:01:05.525 --> 00:01:08.140
Client schedules, travel cost, expiring access,

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.582
or a waiting crew can create pressure to continue.

00:01:10.582 --> 00:01:14.700
Predefined criteria give the pilot a defensible basis for saying no before that pressure

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:15.800
narrows judgment.
